#  ON AUTOMATED LITERATURE SEARCHES. REPO FIRST, NETWORK SECOND.
# =====================================================================
# A seven-reference batch from an automated search, September 2026, was
# checked against this file before anything was fetched. Four of the seven
# were ALREADY CITED here under different names, and three carried errors:
#
#   * "Thompson et al., Pediatr Res 1991;30:135" is breath_test_original,
#     already in this file. Wrong first author (Barshop) and wrong pages
#     (30(1):15-22). The PMID it gave, 1909779, was correct and is what
#     identified the duplicate.
#   * "Attarwala et al., Nat Commun 2024" is mrna_moa, already in this file.
#     Attarwala is not among its eighteen authors; the first author is Baek.
#   * The Nucleic Acid Therapeutics 2023 paper it offered as new is
#     pkpd_translational, already in this file and already cited for exactly
#     the figures the batch reported as a finding.
#
# The lesson is the ordering, not the tool: every identifier in a batch
# should be matched against this file and against refs.bib BEFORE any
# fetch, because a duplicate under a wrong author name is invisible to a
# check that only asks whether an identifier resolves. A PMID is the only
# field in these batches that proved reliable.
#
# =====================================================================
#  NOT YET RESOLVED. Do not cite until an identifier is confirmed.
# =====================================================================
