# --- whole-body propionate: where the load comes from ----------------
# Source partitioning in inborn errors of propionate metabolism.
# "Amino acid catabolism accounted for a mean of 51.7% (range 24.5% to
# 66.4%) of total propionate production"; mean decrease after metronidazole
# 22.2% +/- 8.5 (the gut-flora fraction); ~30% unaccounted for, likely
# odd-chain fatty acid catabolism. This is the primary source for s_base's
# partitioning.
propionate_sources      doi:10.1016/0026-0495(90)90084-P

# Endogenous colonic propionate rate of appearance 0.27 +/- 0.09
# umol/kg/min = ~389 umol/kg/day. Gives the gut fermentation flux in
# absolute units.
colonic_propionate      doi:10.3390/nu7115440

# Metronidazole 10-20 mg/kg/day in 5 MMA + 4 PA children. Mean decrease in
# urinary propionate metabolites 41% (range 12-76, P < 0.01); mean plasma
# propionate 45.0 -> 25.1 umol/l (P < 0.05). Cross-check on the gut fraction.
metronidazole_pa        doi:10.1007/BF01957284

# 3-methylhistidine excretion as an index of muscle proteolysis. Control
# 3.6 umol/kg/day (males); skeletal trauma +280% (males) / +225% (females);
# trauma with steroids +325%; sepsis +227% (males) / +292% (females).
# Bounds the illness amplitude s_peak/s_base from above.
muscle_catabolism       doi:10.1016/0026-0495(81)90022-6

# Mechanism of action across mRNA-3927 (PA), mRNA-3705 (MMA), mRNA-3210
# (PKU), with allometric human scaling. PD responses sustained 3-4 weeks
# after dosing in Pcca-/- mice. Companion to the translational PK/PD model.
#
# ONE FILE REMAINS UNOPENED, and the k_e row is written so that it does not
# matter which way it goes. This paper's SUPPLEMENT has not been read: every
# publisher host is denied at this project's build proxy, and the September
# 2026 pass that read pkpd_translational's Supplementary Table S1 could not
# reach this one. If it carries a fitted kout for 3-HP, that would be a third
# weak anchor alongside the methylmalonic-acid band and the paper is better
# for it; it would NOT overturn the k_e row, which claims the absence of an
# INDEPENDENT MEASUREMENT IN HUMANS, and a constant fitted to murine data
# inside a PK/PD model is model-derived whatever its value. Anyone with
# journal access should open it and record what is there.
mrna_moa                doi:10.1038/s41467-024-47460-9

# The nearest MEASURED analogue for k_e, and it is not 3-HP. Detailed
# kinetics of methylmalonic acid in a 28-year-old mut0 patient: one
# haemodialysis session cut plasma MMA by 54%, giving a plasma clearance of
# 103 mL/min and a volume of distribution of 0.48 L/kg, which approximates
# total body water; MMA then reaccumulated to the pre-dialysis concentration
# within 24 h. CAVEATS, and they are load-bearing: the clearance is DIALYTIC
# and not endogenous, so it bounds the endogenous route from above rather
# than measuring it; and MMA is dicarboxylic with strong tubular handling
# where 3-HP is monocarboxylic (pKa 4.9, MW 90), so this is a plausibility
# band for k_e and not a substitute for measuring it.
ke_mma_analogue         pmid:24961826

# Guidelines for management of PA. Metabolic control judged clinically and
# by ammonia, acid-base and trends in C3, C3/C2 and 2-MC. NOTE: specifies
# NO numeric plasma 3-HP target, which is why m_tol is a convention.
# Metronidazole regimen, verbatim: "10-20 mg/kg/day divided in 2-3 times...
#   1-2 weeks of therapy alternating with 2-3 weeks off or alternating every
#   month is advisable." With metronidazole_pa's 41% this makes the
#   non-enzymatic load a ~40% square wave on a 21-35 day period.
# Dialysis: rebound after intermittent HD is the stated reason for
#   preferring continuous therapy. The one human observation bearing on
#   whether a slow compartment sits behind the plasma pool.
pa_guidelines           doi:10.1186/s13023-014-0130-8

# Newborn dried-blood-spot LC-MS/MS. 99.9th-percentile 3-HP cutoff
# 38.13 umol/L. Nearest quantitative anchor for a population 3-HP scale.
dbs_3hp_cutoff          doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0184897


